/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-18T09:24:45Z","updated_at":"2015-10-18T09:46:04Z","body":"I have checked what are you talking about, and you are right.\nGLM should follow the GLSL convention and handle it's matrices in column-major fashion.\nAccording to that, not only shearZ3D, but all the shear functions (and possibly other transformations) are wrong, because it looks like they are handled in a row-major fashion, which is the transposed.\n\nhttp://www.cs.colorado.edu/~mcbryan/5229.03/mail/55.htm\nhttp://run.usc.edu/cs480-s13/lec05-viewing/05-viewing-6up.pdf\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/148994811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"plasmacel","id":5353968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTM5Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5353968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel","html_url":"https://github.com/plasmacel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pla